      "result": "W",
      "result_description": "Wadebridge CC - 1st XI - Won",
      "result_applied_to": "36578",
      "match_notes": "Wadebridge continued their strong start with a comfortable 71-run success at Ladycross. Inserted on a damp deck in a 45-over contest, James Maycock (24) fought hard against disciplined bowling before Ben Jenkin (2-40) made a double breakthrough. Cal Morse (52) and Charlie McLachlan (39) added 87, but Ian Searle (2-50) and Mark Hodgson (2-45) turned 145-2  into 153-5. With wickets in the bank though, Elliot Dunnett (27*) was able to attack at the death to see the Swans to 208-7. In reply, Stuart Parkyn (2-17) soon caused problems for the Werrington top order, and faced with the difficult task of needing to up the rate against Barny Jackson (2-25) and Alek Gill (3-18), the hosts slid from 48-2 to 62-7. From there, Tom Lyle (54*) nursed the tail with an expert knock to garner another two batting points as Werrington finished on 137-9.",
